{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>If so.</b> It is a stylistic embellishment — to insert a word in the Hebrew manner: 'If so, I am compelled to act — that I should send him with you — I must go back and seek: where is there a remedy and counsel to advise you?' And so I say <b>this do</b>:" "<b>The praise of the land.</b> From the fact that it is praised in the land — that everyone sings of it when it comes into the world." "<b>Mastic.</b> שַׁעֲוָה." "<b>Almonds.</b> I do not know what they are. And in the commentaries of alef-bet by Rabbi Machir I saw פשט\"ציאס, and it seems to me they are אֲפַרְסְקִין."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {3 "The Old French word פשט\"ציאס is Old French pistaces (pistachios); אֲפַרְסְקִין are peaches. Rashi signals uncertainty about both the foreign word and its identification."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:19.879302594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}